+## Offline performance candidate
+
+The next candidate distributes Q8 activation packing across all input columns
+and adds a four-column IMCI panel for Q3_K/Q4_K/Q5_K/Q6_K. Each weight block is
+unpacked once for four prompt tokens. `GGML_KNC_MQ_COLS=1` selects the previous
+row kernel for a same-binary comparison; `4` enables the candidate panel.
+Single-token decode and one-to-three-column tails retain the previous kernel.
+Reference mode, unsupported types, strided tensors and batched outer dimensions
+retain their existing dispatch. No model datatype metadata is rewritten.
+
+`test-panel.py` uses the pinned BluePower instruction translators with ASan/UBSan
+to check the actual assembly equations, alignment, tails, prefetch bounds and
+scaled rounding against independent packed arithmetic and the previous kernel.
+It is a host source-semantics check, not native qualification. The extended
+`test-knc-mq` covers four-column boundaries through the actual graph dispatcher
+and must still run on each matching card before promotion.
+
+`performance-plan.py --plan 7120P --output NEW.json` generates a staged test plan
+without executing it. Plans are available for 3120A, 5110P and 7120P. Run them
+through the existing exclusive workload, thermal, memory and heartbeat guards.
+Screen small models first, then confirm held-out settings on the real target
+model with at least five paired repetitions. `--score RECEIPT.json` rejects host
+timings, unmatched workloads and missing correctness/affinity/guard gates.
+Targets are >=2 decode / >=4 prefill tokens/s for 8B-10B and >=5 / >=8 for 2.6B
+(stretch 6 / 10). These are acceptance targets, not measured results.
+
+The separate PhiChat resident adapter adds a byte-bounded image-embedding LRU,
+content-hash and crop-ordinal keys, independently selected vision threads,
+image-token budgets and separate preparation/encoding/ingestion/text/decode
+timings. It clears decoder and recurrent state between requests. It does not
+reuse conversation KV state, change model quantization or skip reasoning tokens.
+Step3's existing `image_max_tokens` option now selects a complete crop grid when
+it fits, or the existing overview-only path. A budget below the fixed overview
+is rejected. Full detail remains the default; overview mode requires a separate
+visual-quality check for small text and fine detail.
+
+The design follows publicly documented serving techniques, adapted to KNC:
+[TensorRT-LLM's bounded encoder cache](https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/llm-api/reference/MultimodalConfig.html)
+and [multimodal pipeline stages and raw-image hashing](https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/latest/features/multi-modality.html).
+GPU-specific concurrent batching, speculative decoding and approximate visual
+token pruning are not enabled by this change. Operator profiling is opt-in;
+its synchronized timings must not be submitted as throughput evidence.
+
+## Bandwidth goals for the next pass
+
+The requested long-term targets use the 7120P's advertised 352 GB/s divided by
+estimated compressed model size. Treat these as aspirational weight-streaming
+ceilings, not measured performance or an acceptance promise. Intel specifies
+[maximum memory bandwidth](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/products/sku/75799/intel-xeon-phi-coprocessor-7120p-16gb-1-238-ghz-61-core/specifications.html);
+an [empirical roofline](https://amcr.lbl.gov/departments/computer-science-department/ppan/roofline-performance-model/empirical-roofline-tool-ert/)
+also needs attainable bandwidth and compute throughput. KNC quant unpacking,
+scalar scale/reduction instructions, attention and synchronization can limit
+decoding before memory bandwidth is saturated.
+
+The actual 256-weight blocks in `ggml-common.h` use the following storage:
+
+| Tensor type | Bytes/block | Bits/weight including scales |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Q3_K | 110 | 3.4375 |
+| Q4_K | 144 | 4.5 |
+| Q5_K | 176 | 5.5 |
+| Q6_K | 210 | 6.5625 |
+
+`Q3_K_M`, `Q4_K_M` and `Q5_K_M` are mixed tensor recipes, not fixed bit rates.
+Use each GGUF's tensor inventory and the actual active matrices. For example,
+eight billion weights stored uniformly as Q5_K occupy 5.5 decimal GB, giving
+352/5.5 = 64 tokens/s in the idealized weight-only calculation, not 70.4.
+Neither result accounts for the rest of the graph. Whole-file size is especially
+misleading for MoE, which only visits selected experts at each step.
+
+Memory headroom and multimodal decoding require their own measurements. A
+conventional 32-layer decoder with eight KV heads, head dimension 128, FP16 K/V
+and 131,072 cached positions needs 16 GiB for KV alone. That example leaves no
+room for model weights on this card. Image tokens can remain in attention's
+context, and some architectures use cross-attention during generation. Equal
+parameter counts therefore do not imply equal text and image decoding speeds.
+
+After the current paired tests, pursue this sequence without changing the
+working installation:
+
+1. Measure sustained read bandwidth with an IMCI streaming checksum and a working
+   set well above aggregate L2, using each card's admitted worker cores and
+   2/3/4-way SMT. Validate the checksum and retain clock, ECC, affinity and
+   temperature records. Include power and thermal throttle status, turbo state
+   and power samples aligned to each phase. Do not import KNL or GPU bandwidth
+   measurements. Power below the 300 W TDP is a utilization clue, not proof of
+   proportional speed headroom; judge changes by tokens/s and joules/token.
+2. Measure representative Q3/Q4/Q5/Q6 single-token matrix shapes with exact packed
+   data, then compare effective weight traffic with the streaming result. Add
+   separate FP16 attention, reduction and barrier microbenchmarks. A synchronized
+   whole-graph profiler may identify candidates but cannot establish their
+   uninstrumented cost.
+3. Optimize the measured limit: weight loading/unpacking if quantized matrix
+   throughput is low, FP16 vector conversion/dot work if attention dominates,
+   or threadpool work allocation if small operations pay excessive overhead.
+   Preserve packed rounding and evaluate any changed reduction against a
+   matched-input oracle before measuring real-model throughput.
+4. Confirm one change at a time against the preserved runtime with held-out
+   prompts and five alternating pairs. Report prefill and decode separately,
+   then expand context and image-token counts. Keep the immediate >=2/4 and
+   >=5/8 decode/prefill milestones above; revise achievable long-term targets
+   using measured bytes per token and instruction throughput.
+
+Every SKU needs its own native settings and evidence. A 7120P winner is a
+starting configuration for 3120A/5110P, not their qualification.
